course: dictionary
lesson: 8489
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The clues around it tell you which meaning is right. «The children dug a tunnel in the sandpit before lunch.» Dug and children tell you a sandpit is a low box or shallow hole filled with sand for playing in.
explain: The same word can also be used in sport. «The long jumper ran down the track and landed in the sandpit.» Long jumper tells you this sandpit is the sand area where athletes land. Always ask which meaning fits the other words in the sentence.
explain: Context can also tell you what to do. «Mia washed her hands after playing in the sandpit.» Washing hands is a hygiene clue, so sandpits are places where germs can get on your hands. A square sandpit with a side of 3 metres needs 3 × 4 = 12 metres of fence to go all around it.
fact: A sandpit is a low box or shallow hole filled with sand for children to play in.
fact: In sports, a sandpit is the sand area where athletes land in the long jump.
fact: The plural of sandpit is sandpits, meaning more than one.
fact: Wash your hands after playing in the sandpit, and cover it so animals do not use it.
fact: «Stopping slowly is gentler than stopping suddenly», so the soft sand helps a jumper land safely.
exercise: «The children dug a tunnel in the sandpit before lunch.» What is a sandpit in this sentence? | A large lake of water | Only a sandwich shop | A kind of long jump race | *A low box or shallow hole filled with sand for children to play in
exercise: «The long jumper landed in the sandpit with a soft thump.» In this sentence, what is a sandpit? | A type of fence | *The sand area where athletes land in the long jump | A place to wash your hands | A box of sand for playing
exercise: Mia washed her hands after playing in the sandpit. What should you do after playing in a sandpit? | *Wash your hands | Eat your lunch in it | Jump as far as you can | Throw sand at your friends
test: «A square sandpit with a side of 3 metres needs 3 × 4 = 12 metres of fence.» Why does it need 12 metres of fence? | *A square has four sides, each 3 metres long | Fence costs 12 pounds per metre | A sandpit is 12 metres wide | The fence is 12 metres high
test: Which word is the plural of sandpit? | sandpitses | sandpit's | *sandpits | sandpitting
exam: Why is a sandpit a good place to land in the long jump? | *It lets you slow down over a longer time, so the landing is gentler | It is cold and wet | It makes you jump higher | It is hard, so it bounces you back up
